# LIMITS — What is not ready

File: wiki/Limits.oot
User wiki. Canonical URL: https://wiki.openooda.org/#Limits.oot

## 1. How to read this page

If a thing is listed here, do not say it works as product.
Wanted and not built is called residual.

## 2. Install and public site

There is no working public `curl | sh` install.
The compiler tree is private.
The public install script pins an old tag and does not check a hash.
The public fetch 404s.

There is no public playground.

Research papers are design. They are not a running compiler.

## 3. Backends and machines

Native product is emit C, then host `gcc`.

LLVM IR emit of the compiler is product. A `clang` link of the full compiler is residual.

Standalone x86_64 emit is product. AArch64 emit is residual.

WebAssembly emit writes a module. It is not a browser playground.

`GpuCap` on CPU/noop is product. `emit_ptx` writes kernel text. Launching on a real GPU is residual. This is not CUDA.

## 4. Library and proofs

The large org `std/` tree is residual as a certified library.
Named small proves exist. Thousands of files is volume, not a cert.

Const `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` on function headers can fold at check time.
A general SMT solver is residual.

## 5. Security hardware

Process-local capability tokens are product.
Hierarchical HMAC attenuation and measured isolate are product.

SGX, TDX, and SEV hardware enclaves are residual.
Measured isolate is not a hardware enclave.

## 6. Other leftovers people ask about

HITL (a separate human-in-the-loop product) is not shipped.
The human loop is `ooda fix`.

`cargo` / Rust is gone. Do not look for it.

JIT and a 0ms garbage collector are not product.

`ooda test --fuzz` prints a floor line and returns. It is not a fuzzer.

This page is the public limit list.
This wiki: https://wiki.openooda.org
Site: https://openooda.org
